---
// The brand word with its green i-dot. The DOM text is the plain word; the
// ink layer on top is a pseudo-element drawing the dotless "sıtrep", so only
// the tittle shows through. Copy/paste, search and screen readers all see
// just "sitrep" (the pseudo-element carries empty alt text).
//
// The under-layer is not painted flat accent green: at 1x every antialiased
// edge pixel blends the ink overlay with what sits beneath it, and a green
// underlay tints the whole word green (measured - the hero read as a green
// word in a 1x screenshot). Instead the under-layer is a glyph-clipped
// gradient: accent only in the tittle band above the x-height, ink below,
// so edges blend ink-on-ink and only the dot region can show green.
---

<span class="sitrep-wm">sitrep</span>

<style>
  .sitrep-wm {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .sitrep-wm::after {
    content: 'sıtrep' / '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  /* The lh offset skips the half-leading above the glyphs, so the cut sits
     just under the tittle regardless of the inherited line-height. Guarded
     on both features it needs: without the guard, a browser lacking either
     would drop only the background and paint transparent text - an
     invisible brand word. Unsupported browsers keep the flat-green word. */
  @supports (-webkit-background-clip: text) and (height: 1lh) {
    .sitrep-wm {
      color: transparent;
      background: linear-gradient(
        to bottom,
        var(--accent) calc((1lh - 1em) / 2 + 0.42em),
        var(--ink) calc((1lh - 1em) / 2 + 0.42em)
      );
      -webkit-background-clip: text;
      background-clip: text;
    }
  }
  /* Inside a link the wordmark yields to the link: an anchor must read as
     one colour under one continuous underline, and the inline-block box
     alone would break the underline (text decorations do not propagate
     into atomic inline boxes). Declared last so it wins the @supports
     path's transparent-ink treatment too. */
  :global(a) .sitrep-wm {
    display: inline;
    color: inherit;
    background: none;
    -webkit-background-clip: initial;
    background-clip: initial;
  }
  :global(a) .sitrep-wm::after {
    content: none;
  }
</style>
